            <ArticleTitle>Myalgia and cramps associated with zolmitriptan.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>241-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To report a patient with myalgia and cramps possibly induced by the antimigrainous agent zolmitriptan.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE REPORT" NlmCategory="METHODS">A 27-year-old woman with episodes of common migraine developed cramps and generalized myalgia after the use of intranasal zolmitriptan 5 mg to treat 3 episodes of migraine. This side effect had not occurred with oral zolmitriptan 2.5 mg.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Myalgia and cramps should be considered a possible dose-dependent adverse effect of zolmitriptan.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
